# Anti-Patterns - What NOT to Do

## Code Generation
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER generate placeholder/mock data
const companies = [{ id: 1, name: "Test" }]

// ✅ ALWAYS fetch from API or use empty state
const [companies, setCompanies] = useState<Company[]>([])
```

## API Calls
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER use fetch directly in components
const data = await fetch('/api/...')

// ✅ ALWAYS use apiRequest wrapper
const result = await featureApi.getAll()
```

## Error Handling
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER swallow errors silently
try { await api.call() } catch (e) {}

// ✅ ALWAYS handle and show user feedback
try {
  await api.call()
} catch (e) {
  toast({ title: t('error.failed'), variant: 'destructive' })
}
```

## Translations
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER hardcode user-facing strings
<Button>Save Changes</Button>

// ✅ ALWAYS use translation keys
<Button>{t('common.save')}</Button>
```

## State Management
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER store derived state
const [filteredItems, setFilteredItems] = useState([])

// ✅ ALWAYS compute derived values
const filteredItems = useMemo(() => 
  items.filter(i => i.status === filter), [items, filter]
)
```

## TypeScript
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER use `any`
const data: any = response

// ✅ ALWAYS type properly or use `unknown`
const data: Company = response.data
```

## MongoDB IDs
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER assume id exists
company.id

// ✅ ALWAYS handle both _id and id
const companyId = company._id || company.id
```
